4. Row Level Security (RLS)
Since this is a single-user personal app, RLS is simple:
code
SQL
-- Enable RLS on all tables
ALTER TABLE user_profile ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE conversations ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE messages ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE memory_entries ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE gemini_model_config ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE api_usage_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE whatsapp_messages ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE zara_settings ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Policy: Only service role (backend) can access everything
-- Anon key gets no direct access (backend proxies all DB calls)
-- Note: ChatGPT will implement exact RLS policies per Supabase best practices
Security approach: Frontend never calls Supabase directly for sensitive data. Backend (Node.js) uses SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY for all data operations. Frontend's VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is for auth only (if needed in future).
